think Standfast: read crux/REDS.md whole. Every living row is CLOSED or RELEASED (80, 81, 82, 83, 85, 86, 87, 74, 78); only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a history rewrite = custody gate #1). No open agent-closable red -- the line is clear to take new constructive work.
think Crux-first pick: the centroid log named render leaves (extended-maxima, size-histogram) and a fetch-gated photo top-hat. A survey of image/*.rye showed the whole segmentation family (label, distance, regions, centroid, watershed, segment) consumes a binary MASK a fixture draws by hand -- and nothing MAKES a mask from a real image by an adaptive threshold. The skeleton readers binarize at a FIXED red>=128. The missing crux is the FRONT DOOR: an intensity histogram plus Otsu's method (1979), highest-Lindy (it opens the front of the pipeline, every downstream reader already built), a genuine measurement plus a real optimization, agent-doable with a synthetic bimodal fixture -- no fetch gate.
think Composition read: hitmiss.binarize and branch.is_on fix the mask convention (opaque white/black, alpha pinned, red>=128 foreground); photos.luma_of is Rec.601 (77/150/29, sum 256) but lives in the high-level Photos app, so I owned a small local luma projection in the primitive rather than invert the dependency -- exactly as hitmiss owns its binarize.
think Designed the decisive crux before coding: a DARK bimodal image (gray-40 and gray-90, both below 128) where the fixed 128 cut calls the whole image background (empty mask) yet Otsu splits at 40 so the bright hump alone lights; and a BRIGHT bimodal (gray-160 and gray-220, both above 128) where the fixed cut calls everything foreground yet Otsu splits at 160. Otsu adapts where a fixed cut fails -- the whole reason the front door exists.
think Otsu metric in f64 (as color.rye already uses f64) for the argmax only -- integer histogram and class sums in u64, the between-class variance w0*w1*(mu0-mu1)^2 compared for the max; the lowest maximizer wins (strict greater-than update) so the pick is deterministic on the flat valley of an ideal bimodal image. Hand-traced both fixtures to the exact threshold (40 and 160) before the build.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal run, no reds: the HISTOGRAM crux (two humps of eight, no spurious bin), the OTSU-VALLEY crux (dark splits at 40, bright at 160, each against the failing fixed-128 contrast rendered by the same threshold_mask_at), the UNIFORM crux (a single tone returns 0, marks all foreground -- the honest degenerate), the QOI round-trip byte-for-byte, EmptySource refusal by name having allocated nothing, determinism byte-for-byte.
obs Compose not braid: the module OWNS only the luma projection, the histogram tally, and the between-class-variance search; qoi owns the RGBA buffers, the mask reads downstream through branch.is_on. threshold_mask_at is the one renderer the Otsu path and a caller-chosen threshold share, so the split is defined the same way everywhere.
obs Gates all GREEN: tools/threshold_witness.rish GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean; width-check exit 0; plain 7-bit ASCII; living_docs_lint advisory-only GREEN; living_card_ascii_witness GREEN. image/README.md Threshold (automatic, Otsu) bullet after Centroid, named as the family's front door (docs-sync). REMEMBER repointed single-stranded, centroid folded to a one-line prior-nib pointer (no cairn -- a one-line repoint).
obs Council rota lap deep-read foundations/20260814-071700_hardware-and-right-to-repair.md (item 6) -- "Open underneath: every image rests in an open format the tree owns end to end." This rung is exactly that promise's front: a real image becomes a countable shape through our own open geometry, no proprietary threshold, nothing a reader cannot check.
